Iminoboranes $( \mathrm { R B } { \equiv } \mathrm { N R } ^ { \prime } )$ are isoelectronic with alkynes and also readily undergo addition, polymerization, and other reactions. However, the methods for synthesizing iminoboranes are very limited, which to some extent restricts their applications. In 2021, research teams from Southern University of Science and Technology and Nankai University jointly developed an efficient iminoborane transfer reagent $\mathrm{X}$.

Heating $4.84 ~ \mathrm { g } ~ \mathrm { D m p B B r } _ { 2 }$ and $0.25 ~ \mathrm { g } ~ \mathrm { L i N H _ { 2 } }$ to $100 ^ { \circ } \mathrm { C }$, followed by solvent evaporation, yields $\mathrm{A}$. A peak in its mass spectrum (corresponding to $[ \pmb { \mathrm { A } } ] ^ { + } ) \ m / z = 420.1$. Reacting $0.420 \textrm { g } \mathrm{A}$ with $0.335 ~ \mathrm { g } ~ \mathrm { L i H M D S }$ in benzene at room temperature for half an hour allows the isolation of $0.236 \ \mathrm { g }$ of white powder $\mathrm{X}$, with a yield of approximately $45 \%$. The theoretical mass fraction of Br is $30.80 \%$.  

[Dmp: 2,6-bis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)phenyl; LiHMDS: lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide]  

$\mathrm{X}$ can exhibit the properties of iminoboranes and be used to synthesize heterocycles. Reacting $0.048 ~ g$ of pivaloyl chloride with $0.210 ~ g ~ \mathrm{X}$ yields $0.092 ~ g$ of an eight-membered ring compound $\mathrm{B}$; when $\mathrm{X}$ reacts with an excess of trimethylsilyl azide, $\mathrm{C}$ is obtained.  

Which of the following statements are correct?  

1. $\mathrm{A}$ contains 2 $\mathrm{Br}$ atoms;  
2. The sum of atoms in the chemical formula of $\mathrm{X}$ is 56;  
3. The yield of $\mathrm{B}$ is $55 \%$;  
4. $\mathrm{C}$ contains a six-membered ring;  
5. $\mathrm{C}$ has a $C_2$ axis.

